{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel","id":1402680,"title":"Lex Magica, and Time Travel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-13T14:16:31-07:00","id":1402680,"title":"Lex Magica, and Time Travel","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> What is the Lex Magica position on crimes committed and unmade with time travel?<br /> <br /> Let say Jack commits a crime (no petty theft, something seriously bad: murder or rape of sleepers, soul-eating) and uses Shifting Sands with reach to go back a couple of hours before anything happened. The Consilium finds out (mind-reading, post cognition; doesn't matter how, the thing is they find out); Jack's defense is that nothing actually happened, whatever he did was undone when he used Shifting Sands.<br /> <br /> Will the Consilium condemn him? What are the charges? There are no victims since that timeline did not come to pass, but he reaped the benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-13-2020, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T15:09:47-07:00","id":1402692,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, this is going to fall into the &quot;who has jurisdiction?&quot; bin.<br /> The two orders that have the most interest in such a figure as I see it are:<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder, because Jack is screwing up his soul, even if he's figured out how to make his crimes victimless.(And one <i>could</i> play with eternality of souls and have a mystery spring up from memories transmitted outside of time.)<br /> The Guardians of the Veil tend to police mages, in general. They would probably just monitor the guy and, if he breaks a law, drop the axe.<br /> <br /> In any Pentacle order are individuals who'd not mind or defend the acts and those who'd condemn it. Legally, though, it's likely fair game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T10:19:38-07:00","id":1402826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1402692#post1402692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, this is going to fall into the &quot;who has jurisdiction?&quot; bin.<br /> The two orders that have the most interest in such a figure as I see it are:<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder, because Jack is screwing up his soul, even if he's figured out how to make his crimes victimless.(And one <i>could</i> play with eternality of souls and have a mystery spring up from memories transmitted outside of time.)<br /> The Guardians of the Veil tend to police mages, in general. They would probably just monitor the guy and, if he breaks a law, drop the ax.<br /> <br /> In any Pentacle order are individuals who'd not mind or defend the acts and those who'd condemn it. Legally, though, it's likely fair game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ok, I totally buy the Guardians thinking it is their jurisdiction = Abusing magic; and I agree that they would monitor, if he breaks a law, kill him for it, no time to &quot;undo the damage&quot;.<br /> <br /> I also see the Mysterium: if your crime is going to an Atheneum, copying all the grimoires in your head and traveling back in time; for them that IS a big crime, since information in Mage can time-travel.<br /> <br /> Free Council would think &quot;This guy is an asshole&quot;, and the more militant Free Councilors might deal with this person permanently, just like the Guardians.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But my question was more about what is the Lex position on this type of crime. I can go, rape up your spouse/beat the annoying sleeper neighbor/torture my political rival for a day, and then time travel back, no consequences if found, except that you might be disturbed/angry about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-22-2020, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T10:32:51-07:00","id":1402831,"title":"","content":"It's might be violation of the Precept of Hubris regardless. The point of that precept is as much to prevent the mage from falling to hubris as it is to prevent others from becoming the mage's victims. The use of Shifting Sands may be seen as an attempt to conceal the crime that would compound the violation.<br /> <br /> But remember that the Lex Magica is not a moral code. Suppose that the murder of a Sleeper was performed via a Legacy attainment and it served as part of a legitimate magical experiment. That may not be a violation of Lex Magica. Part of the horror aspect of Mage is that mage society tolerates obsessions that are harmful to Sleepers, so long as they don't endanger the Awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T11:04:28-07:00","id":1402837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1402831#post1402831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's might be violation of the Precept of Hubris regardless. The point of that precept is as much to prevent the mage from falling to hubris as it is to prevent others from becoming the mage's victims. The use of Shifting Sands may be seen as an attempt to conceal the crime that would compound the violation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood this part.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1402831#post1402831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But remember that the Lex Magica is not a moral code.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this, it is a legal code.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1402831#post1402831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose that the murder of a Sleeper was performed via a Legacy attainment and it served as part of a legitimate magical experiment. That may not be a violation of Lex Magica. Part of the horror aspect of Mage is that mage society tolerates obsessions that are harmful to Sleepers, so long as they don't endanger the Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I am wrong, but doesn't the Lex have provisions to protect sleepers and usage of magic to hurt them is an aggravation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-22-2020, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T11:16:15-07:00","id":1402838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1402837#post1402837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I am wrong, but doesn't the Lex have provisions to protect sleepers and usage of magic to hurt them is not an aggravant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for the sake of the Sleepers, but only insofar as it helps protect the Awakened and supernal phenomenon. The main purpose of the Lex Magica is to enshrine the right of individual mages to pursue mysteries and obsessions, limiting that right only where it results in conflict with other mages. It's not about protecting sleepers, it's about arbitrating conflicts between mages.<br /> <br /> Morals are for mortals, to quote DaveB. Mage is a horror game, not a superhero game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Think of the Lex Magica as mage's counterpart to the Traditions from Vampire. The Lex isn't about defending Sleepers any more than the Traditions are about defending Kine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 07-14-2020, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T23:59:09-07:00","id":1402916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1402838#post1402838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not for the sake of the Sleepers, ...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Think of the Lex Magica as mage's counterpart to the Traditions from Vampire. The Lex isn't about defending Sleepers any more than the Traditions are about defending Kine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Individual magi will certainly be interested in policing the problem, but the Lex? It's not likely to have a law against that unless <i>heavily </i>Silver Ladder influenced and even then it would almost certainly only be considered a bronze law violation. If it isn't interfering with a Mystery someone is snooping into, who's got the standing to object? (That Silver Ladder Lictor probably thinks he does.)<br /> <br /> Careless murders invite Sleeper witness to the affairs of magi. Those are illegal.<br /> Murders outside of time? Be careful not to create paradoxes. Don't go driving yourself mad. Many magi would find it distasteful. Quite a few would try to put a stop to it. Willing to start a mage feud over it, though? That's the sticking point.<br /> <br /> For such disputes, the duel arcane was invented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T04:02:55-07:00","id":1402927,"title":"","content":"It doesn't really matter if Lex isn't a moral code, mages are still humans. They're going to care about you doing horrific things to people. The Lex was made by people. People who don't want the people they care about and the communities they live in to have serial killers and psychos doing messed up things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 07-15-2020, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T04:20:23-07:00","id":1402929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1402927#post1402927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't really matter if Lex isn't a moral code, mages are still humans. They're going to care about you doing horrific things to people. The Lex was made by people. People who don't want the people they care about and the communities they live in to have serial killers and psychos doing messed up things.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact mages are human no more, their integrity <br /> has shattered and they have wisdom in its place.<br /> Some of them may still care, but they lose the natural instinct that generates empathy, they are led by obsessions.<br /> Lex magica exist only as a way to protect mage society, and laws that concern humans safeguard exist because a lot of abused sleepers could attract unwanted attention","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T06:59:11-07:00","id":1402941,"title":"","content":"That is painfully wrong. Mages don't lose their natural empathy instincts at all. They have obsession riding on top of their minds, but part of the whole point of mages horror is that they're just normal people with power and a tendency for obsession. Cutting out their empathy like that is completely just headcanon on your part.<br /> <br /> Integrity and empathy aren't even related for godsake. @_@","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 07-15-2020, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T07:30:46-07:00","id":1402943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1402941#post1402941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is painfully wrong. Mages don't lose their natural empathy instincts at all. They have obsession riding on top of their minds, but part of the whole point of mages horror is that they're just normal people with power and a tendency for obsession. Cutting out their empathy like that is completely just headcanon on your part.<br /> <br /> Integrity and empathy aren't even related for godsake. @_@</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe i exagerated it a bit, but what i meant was that lex magica was invented putting mage interests first, and sleeper s in second place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T08:09:34-07:00","id":1402948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1402941#post1402941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cutting out their empathy like that is completely just headcanon on your part.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can agree that it's not an intrinsic part of Awakening, I should point out that replacing Integrity with Wisdom has two potential consequences for a reduced rating, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1062344-grimoire-of-cursory-dissection-a-thread-for-personal-musings?p=1361021#post1361021\">one of which is</a> &quot;you automatically fail Empathy rolls, gain 'Selfish' as an extra Vice, and replace one of your Obsessions with 'Dominate Others' until you hurt someone you care about in increasingly excessive ways,&quot; and that one's the stickier of the two.<br /> <br /> Mages may not be intrinsically unempathetic, but they sure as hell adopt the attitude easily enough, and the Order that devised the Lex Magica is also the one that has historically said &quot;Hubris is a coward's word.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T14:33:13-07:00","id":1402985,"title":"","content":"The same group which is primarily focused on raising humanity out of the grips of the lie. Hubris is a cowards word not because &quot;fuck the sleepers&quot; but because the silver ladder is founded on the idea that humanity deserves divinity, and the idea that you are a god or deserve the power of the gods is the most core hubris.<br /> <br /> And yes, wisdom falling can lead to immensely unempathetic behaviour, but it's also harder to have fall than Integrity and falls from doing the unempathetic behaviour. If mages we as callous and unempathetic as presented in this thread, most mages would be wisdom 3 and below rather than the official statement that most mages are Understanding level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 07-15-2020, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T16:30:21-07:00","id":1403003,"title":"","content":"That's a circular argument because it assumes that Wisdom is a measure of &quot;common&quot; morality. It's not though.<br /> <br /> Wisdom reflects how careful a mage is with supernal magic. It only declines due reckless actions (acts of hubris) that involve magic or supernal phenomenon. The key factors are (1) how likely the action is to have consequences that the mage didn't intend or can't control and that could bite her in the ass, and (2) how severe those consequences might be.<br /> <br /> Note that use of legacy attainments never provoke degeneration checks. It's because legacy attainments aren't supernal magic -- they're intrinsic (&quot;template&quot;) powers of a mage similar to Vampire Disciplines. That's also why they require two pages of text to outline all their many exceptions to the normal rules for supernal spells. The point here is that degeneration checks occur because of the use of supernal magic, not because of mundane actions, no matter how &quot;evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also note that in the Wisdom system a premeditated,cold-blooded murder is a less severe example offense than a murder undertaken in a fit of rage. In a court of law it would be the opposite, yeah? Crime of passion and all? But for a mage, the calculated murder is less likely to have consequences the mage didn't intend and so it's considered less egregious.<br /> <br /> High Wisdom mages risk degeneration from any unnecessary use of magic because using magic at all is inherently risky and prone to unforeseen consequences despite the best laid plans of mice and men.<br /> <br /> To compare Wisdom to Humanity from Vampire: Wisdom reflects the battle between Man and Magic, while Humanity reflects the battle between Man and The Beast. Vampires retain Humanity by resisting the urges of the The Beast, and Mages retain Wisdom by resisting the urge to use magic indiscriminately/impulsively.<br /> <br /> The bottom line is: Don't interpret Wisdom as some good/evil or nice/mean spectrum. It's not. It's an alien code of behavior for beings who have transcended humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 07-15-2020, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T16:38:47-07:00","id":1403005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1403003#post1403003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that use of legacy attainments never provoke degeneration checks. It's because legacy attainments aren't supernal magic -- they're intrinsic (&quot;template&quot;) powers of a mage similar to Vampire Disciplines. That's also why they require two pages of text to outline all their many exceptions to the normal rules for supernal spells. The point here is that degeneration checks occur because of the use of supernal magic, not because of mundane actions, no matter how &quot;evil.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not because Wisdom only measures use of Supernal magic. It's because the mage's soul is literally reshaped by their Legacy so that actions taken through the personal truth you understand in your Legacy can never be unwise. In short, having a Legacy inures you to Acts of Hubris that would've been caused by your Legacy. Mundane actions very much can cause Acts of Hubris. If you kill a guy it really doesn't matter if you used a gun or a wand (unless you're somehow only triggering the &quot;used magic for something you could've done mundanely&quot; AoH).<br /> <br /> Though, as noted, how you use your magic is very much a huge part of Wisdom. It's just not exclusively what Wisdom is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T17:45:04-07:00","id":1403021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402680-lex-magica-and-time-travel?p=1403005#post1403005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not because Wisdom only measures use of Supernal magic. It's because the mage's soul is literally reshaped by their Legacy so that actions taken through the personal truth you understand in your Legacy can never be unwise. In short, having a Legacy inures you to Acts of Hubris that would've been caused by your Legacy. Mundane actions very much can cause Acts of Hubris. If you kill a guy it really doesn't matter if you used a gun or a wand (unless you're somehow only triggering the &quot;used magic for something you could've done mundanely&quot; AoH).<br /> <br /> Though, as noted, how you use your magic is very much a huge part of Wisdom. It's just not exclusively what Wisdom is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you able to substantiate this?<br /> <br /> The very first lines of the description of Wisdom:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;Wisdom is a mage\u2019s ability to judge the value of when, where, why, and how to use magic. Mages commonly call this virtue sophia, but Awakened society debates constantly on what constitutes \u201cright\u201d usage of their magic.&quot;</div>So then I don't know why someone would think it has to do with something other than that. Those statements set the context for all the subsequent elucidation so that the text doesn't need to include &quot;with magic&quot; in every other sentence.<br /> <br /> Regarding what you wrote about legacy attainments: You can use a legacy attainment in direct opposition to the ethos/philosophy of the legacy, and it still doesn't result in a degeneration roll. For example, a member of the Awakening Gambit could use a legacy attainment to harm a Sleeper with the intent and effect of preventing them from Awakening. Explain how that's consistent with the &quot;personal truth you understand in your Legacy.&quot; No, the only thing that matters here with respect to Wisdom is that the legacy attainments aren't Supernal magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 07-15-2020, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T18:16:52-07:00","id":1403027,"title":"","content":"You're taking a single line and basing your entire understanding on it. Wisdom <i>is</i> a measure of how the mage uses magic, and it ties back into how well the mage deals with Paradox. But it's not <i>exclusively</i> about the mage's magic. Nowhere does it state that only spells can cause Acts of Hubris.<br /> <br /> &quot;In an Act of Hubris, the mage kills a living being for Mana.&quot;<br /> Blood sacrifices are not made through spells.<br /> <br /> &quot;Two mages in nearly identical circumstances cast the same spell <i>or commit the same action</i>, but to one, his Wisdom is safe while the other risks degeneration.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When innocent bystanders are affected by your <br /> character\u2019s spells <i>or actions</i>, she is at risk as well.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Self-mutilating events such as soul stone creation risk degeneration.&quot;<br /> Soul stones are not created through spells. They're results of an innate ability.<br /> <br /> &quot;allowing a Supernal being to be consumed by the Fallen World&quot;<br /> AoH through inaction. No spell is used for this.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>If</i> a mage suffers Wisdom loss <i>through use of a spell</i>, she can choose to wipe that spell from future Acts of Hubris;&quot;<br /> Implying Wisdom loss through means other than spells. If only spells could cause AoH, there would not be need for any clarification that Inurement only applies to spells.<br /> <br /> &quot;Using a Legacy Attainment is never considered an Act of Hubris; <i>the mage\u2019s mystic self is completely attuned to their use.</i>&quot;<br /> A mage's mystic self is not attuned to any mundane actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T22:05:22-07:00","id":1403042,"title":"","content":"Supernal Magic is broader than spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Mana, soul stones, supernal beings, are all supernal phenomenon. They're all magical. Degeneration in those cases falls neatly under my thesis that acts of hubris always involve the mage's interactions with spells and other supernal phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Both of your items keying off the word &quot;action&quot; are cases I had in mind where the authors don't want to write &quot;with magic&quot; a hundred times in that section. Relevant actions in that context would be the activation of an imbued item, the summoning of a supernal being, flaring a nimbus, etc... and this covers the remainder of your points too. Those aren't referring to mundane actions, unless of course the ST wants to make use of the flex built into the Wisdom system to make it so and blunt the horror build into the mage template.<br /> <br /> You didn't address how your interpretation of &quot;mystic self&quot; for legacy attainments makes any sense in light of my point above about there being no exceptions for usages of legacy attainments that are &quot;immoral&quot; (according to a Western concept of morality? Eastern? Atlantean?) and also run utterly counter to the fundaments of the legacy. In no sense would a mage's &quot;mystic self&quot; be attuned to such actions... yet they're degeneration free anyway. It's just a nonsense position. You may as well say that they're free of risk of degeneration <i>because reasons</i>. A legacy is not defined by its attainments; the attainments arise out of and in support of the ethos of the legacy.<br /> <br /> Thematically, Wisdom and the Lex Magica being divorced from the common man's perception of morality is a fundamental driver of horror in Mage. A mage of Enlightened Wisdom could be a stone-cold murderer as long he's very careful, calculating, and judicious in how he employs magic, and the letter of the Lex Magica won't necessarily find him culpable for anything so long as his actions don't step on any other mage's toes. Once you've signed your name to a Watchtower, your God is magic and your morality is all about showing it proper respect.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To clarify, this is the meaning of &quot;mystic self is completely attuned to their use&quot;:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;The mage invokes them from her reshaped soul <b>instead of reaching into the Supernal</b>.&quot;</div>It means that they're effects that arise from the mage's own soul and are not supernal magic. And so, of course, their use has no impact on Wisdom, because Wisdom is only concerned with the mage's actions related to Supernal magic and other Supernal phenomenon. This is the interpretation of this collection of rules that is internally consistent. The other interpretation that you're advocating strikes me as &quot;It doesn't risk degeneration to give it an attractive gameplay advantage, even though that stands in contradiction to the setting.&quot; Going by your interpretation, the game should only have allowed legacy attainments to be degeneration free when the use aligns with the ethos of the legacy.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Honestly, I just don't get why someone would interpret Wisdom as reflecting even in part a common notion of morality/consience, as if a comprehensible character would ever think &quot;Mudering babies is deeply wrong... but I'm cool with it as long as I use this inured spell or legacy attainment. Then my sense of morality isn't violated so no risk of degeneration!&quot; That's just... random. What does make sense though is a character thinking &quot;My provincial notions of morality have burned away in the fires of Supernal Truth, but I must employ these Truths judiciously lest they consume me completely.&quot; In that paradigm, the mage's Wisdom isn't bothered by baby-murdering regardless; the only true sin is the reckless use of magic. That's consistent and comprehensible. A guy doesn't become a Rapt because he got drunk and shot his wife. He becomes a Rapt by using magic so carelessly that he loses all ability to take care in its use. Morals are for mortals.<br /> <br /> Now, this isn't to say that a mage wouldn't feel moral qualms about baby-murdering. We still have to have sympathetic, relatable characters. It's just that these violations of conscience and moral qualms aren't relevant for the Wisdom stat. The bottom line is that Mage does not have a stat that tracks a Good vs. Evil scale, it has a stat that tracks the Judicious vs Reckless scale with respect to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> EDIT 3: But at this point what I really want is for Satchel to prove me wrong by referencing a part of a 2E Mage fiction where a character struggles with Wisdom after a hit-and-run accident, or a DaveB 2E liveplay where he makes someone roll for degeneration after robbing someone at gunpoint, or similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 07-16-2020, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet"